{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/360943-egypt-and-prometheans","id":360943,"title":"Egypt and Prometheans","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-05T21:47:02-08:00","id":360943,"title":"Egypt and Prometheans","content":"In <span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><i>Strange Alchemies</i> on pages 38-39 the book talks about how there are ancient Pandorans in Egypt and that many Nepri who visit Egypt do not return. There is also a rumor that Osiris is still around. If you had to develop Egypt as a setting for characters to visit</span> how would you develop it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4586-vedic","name":"Vedic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T02:28:21-08:00","id":361108,"title":"","content":"I'd probably link Ancient Egypt with a powerful order of Alchemists who ruled as sorcerer kings, although hint that they were poor imitations of a much earlier civilization that held a much greater command over the essence of life to shout out to my Mummy: the Curse fans, and use real world Hermeticism to flavor some of the more modern day Alchemists the Promethean's might run into in Egypt. Next flavor some biblical plagues as the effects of Disquiet, have ancient tombs be guarded by dormant Pandorans, and top it all off with a Sebek Sablimati that claims to be the Egyption deity who hunts for Osiris so that he can devour the rest of him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T22:13:02-08:00","id":363208,"title":"","content":"Thanks, that's very helpful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4586-vedic","name":"Vedic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T01:46:25-08:00","id":363282,"title":"","content":"For gonzo fun, assume the Sphinx is a giant, dormant Praecipitarii. Constant attention keeps it dormant and they even carved a new face over the old one but all it'll take is a throng getting too close and it'll wake up...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T22:50:13-08:00","id":365123,"title":"","content":"&quot;You can't go too far into the desert,&quot; Thatcher says; as she turns to point, the camp fire illuminates her face and for but a moment it is naught but rough muscle and straw-man stitches. &quot;They wake up.&quot;<br /> &quot;Pandorans?&quot; Theo asks. He asks questions, the stupid kind, sitting on a rock in front of a camel-dung fire, because his creator gave him the surname &quot;Soph&quot; and told him to seek wisdom in all things.<br /> He's currently in Egypt trying to understand, exactly, what wisdom is.<br /> &quot;Sure,&quot; Thatcher says. &quot;Or the gods.&quot;<br /> &quot;There are gods here?&quot; Theo asks with a sneer.<br /> Thatcher doesn't take the bait, but throws more fuel to the fire and stares at it, listens to the pop. &quot;Let me tell you a thing,&quot; she says. &quot;When I was young and moronic, much like present company, I decided to come to the cradle of civilization. I thought I'd find the cradle of the Pilgrimage here, too, a thing that tells us a higher truth.&quot;<br /> Theo squirms in his seat, rubs at the stitch-line around his left wrist - he is made of precisely two people, one perfect and the other with only a perfect hand, and he does not like how Thatcher calls him names and then speaks deeper truths.<br /> &quot;So I come here and a patchwork man told me 'do not into the desert go.' Do you know what I do? I go into desert. Pandorans wake up, yes,&quot; and she looks back, away from the campfire again, the stars tossed above the sand dunes like so many glass vials, each a different potion waiting to pour out. Theo wishes they would, finally. &quot;Azoth calls to Azoth. The gods wake up, too.&quot;<br /> &quot;What are they like?&quot; he asks, and then she really looks at him, Measures him, tears through his meager shell of pretension and ideals, wheat-chaff.<br /> &quot;One was like you or I. Missing his,&quot; she is uncomfortable for the first time all night, &quot;his man-parts. Old. Tired. Confused. I think this, this whole Egypt, is the Wasteland and the Wastes to which he went. He follows copper.&quot;<br /> &quot;One?&quot; Theo says.<br /> &quot;The others were like us, too,&quot; Thatcher whispers. &quot;No-one replaced his man-parts, though. Someone replaced the other god's missing parts. Animal heads. Hateful eyes. You'll wake Pandorans in the desert, yes, but you'll wake their gods, too.&quot;<br /> ____<br /> <br /> I like the idea of a Promethean walking into a dark alley and it becoming terribly nightmare-wonderland-ish because of biting pavement and rocks with claws. I'd run Egypt like a Pandoran minefield - you don't know who drove what beneath the sands, and I think some truly old Prometheans could be calling the whole place &quot;Wasteland&quot; (which, in turn, could make some really bizarre and interesting stories - Prometheans die eventually, of old age, but having one or two just hanging on by going to the Wastes at the utter-edges of the world is almost too good a chance for me to pass up).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}